@852. "Blessed and holy is he"... (Revelation 20:6)... He is said to be "holy" who has illustration in Divine truths by conjunction with the Lord...

@861. To "encompass the camp of the saints" (Revelation 20:9) = to obsess and to want to destroy all things of the New Church. @862.

@879. The New Jerusalem is called "holy" (Revelation 21:2) from the Lord, who alone is holy; and from the Divine truths which are in it from the Lord out of the Word...

@948. "He that is holy let him be sanctified still" (Revelation 22:11) = that he who is in truths will be still more in truths.

