@1949. "Horses"... = intellectual things.

@2015[9]. "The white horse" (Revelation 19) = the understanding of truth; and "He that sat upon the horse" = the Word. @2162[5]. @2799[4]. @3448[4].

@2179[2]. When horses appear, they know that the Angels are discoursing about intellectual things.

@2336[6]. Under <Hoof>, see this reference. @2686. @4966[2]. @6015[4].

@2383[2]. "Horse," here (Zechariah 12:4), and elsewhere in the Word, = what is intellectual: hence it is said that "the horse should be smitten with amazement;" and that "the horse of the peoples should he smitten with blindness;" that is, should be filled up with Falsities.

@2686[4]. "The white horse" (Revelation 19) = wisdom. ( = the understanding of the Word as to its interiors. @2760[2]. @2761. Fully Explained.)

@2761. "A horse" = the Intellectual. Illustrated.

@--. "A horse" (Genesis 49:17) = the understanding of the Word.

@--[2]. "Horses" (Habakkuk 3:8, 15) = the Divine truths which are in the Word... "Horses" are here attributed to God, as in the Apocalypse above...

@--[4]. "The bells of the horses" (Zechariah 14:20) = the understanding of the spiritual things of the Word, which are holy.

@--[7]. "Horse" (Zechariah 12:4) manifestly = understanding, which should be "smitten with amazement and blindness."

@--[end]. "We will not ride upon a horse" (Hosea 14:3)... "A horse" = Own intelligence.

@2762. That "a horse" = what is intellectual... comes from the representatives (there). Horses are frequently seen in the World of Spirits, and this with much variety; and also those who are seated on horses; and whenever they appear, they = what is intellectual... It is from the representative of a horse, as being what is intellectual, that when "horses" are mentioned in the Word, the Spirits and Angels who are with the man at once know that it is what is intellectual that is being treated of. Hence, too, it is, that to certain Spirits... when, having been imbued with intelligence and wisdom, they are being elevated into Heaven, there appear bright horses, as it were fiery... (@8029.) @WH 3.

@--[2]. The doctrine of faith was represented by "the fiery horses" (of Elijah); and the doctrine of faith is the same as the understanding of the Word as to its interiors, or as to the internal sense.

@--[3]. See <Chariot>. @--[4]. @AC 5044[8]. @--[9]. @5321[4]. @--[5]. @--[6]. @--[9]. @--[12]. @5354[7]. @5945. @6125[5]. @6212[2]. @6978[2]. @7297[3]. @8029[end]. @8156. @8210. @8332. @9393[3]. @10406[7]. @WH 3. @DLife 30[2]. @AR 437. @875. @CL 42[2]. @76[2]. @--[end]. @103[2]. @TCR 185[2]. @451[end]. @SE 302. @1318. @2275. @2276. @2862. @4707. @AE 175[5]. @208[7]. @355[4]. @--[16]. @1155.

@--. They who have been resuscitated... see represented to them a youth sitting on a horse, and afterwards dismounting from the horse; by which is signified that they are to be instructed in the Knowledges of good and truth before they can come into Heaven. References.

@--[4]. The signification of a horse, as being what is intellectual, was derived from the Ancient Church to the wise... even into Greece. Hence when they described the sun, by which is signified love, they stationed therein the god of their wisdom and intelligence, and attributed to him a chariot and four fiery horses; and when they described the god of the sea - as by the sea are signified knowledges in general - they allotted horses also to him. And when they described the rise of knowledges from what is intellectual, they feigned a flying horse, which burst open a fountain with his hoof, where were the virgins who were knowledges. And nothing else was signified by the Trojan horse, than a production of their art from the understanding to destroy walls...

@2781[3]. "The horse, mule, camel, and donkey" (Zechariah 14:15) = the intellectual things with man, which should be "smitten with the plague."

@2799[14]. "The captivity of the horses" (Amos 4:10) = the Intellectual deprived of its gift. ( = a seduced Intellectual. @7668[3].)

@2826[10]. "The strength of a horse" (Psalms 147:10) = Own power of thinking truth. "A horse" = what is intellectual.

@3217. When the Angels are discoursing about what is intellectual, then in the World of Spirits below them... there appear horses; and these of a size, form, colour, and posture, in agreement with the ideas which the Angels have about what is intellectual. They also have various trappings. There is also a place at some depth and a little to the right, which is called the abode of the intelligent, where horses continually appear; and this because they are in thought about what is intellectual... Hence it is evident... that "the horses" mentioned in the Word = intellectual things. @5321[4]. @WH 3.

@3708[11]. "Horses" = intellectual things; thus the understanding of the doctrinals of good.

@3881[7]. "The horse which shall be smitten with amazement," and "the horse of the peoples with blindness" = Own intelligence.

@3901[3]. "Horses" (Ezekiel 17:15) = what is intellectual (derived from scientifics).

@--[8]. "Horses" (of the Chaldeans) (Habakkuk 1:8) = their intellectual things which are of like quality.

@3923[2]. "Biting the heels of the horse" (Genesis 49:1 7) = consulting the lowest intellectual or scientific things, and forming conclusions thence.

@--[4]. "The snorting of the horses was heard from Dan" (Jeremiah 8:16) = ratiocination about truth from what is not affirmative.

@4966[2]. The horse (Pegasus) was what is intellectual. @7729[end].

@--. Horses were attributed to the sun, to signify intellectual things from celestial love.

@5113[12]. "Horses" (Revelation 14:20) = intellectual things.

@5319[end]. That "the white horse" = the internal sense of the Word. References. Hence "white horses" (Revelation 19:14) = truths from the Divine; for all things of the internal sense of the Word are truths from the Divine; on which account His armies were seen upon white horses...

@5321[3]. "Horses," in the Word, = intellectual things. @7729[2].

@5354[7]. "Horse" = what is intellectual. References. @10227[9].

@5895[4]. "Will horses run upon the rock?" (Amos 6:12) = whether the truth of faith will be understood.

@--. "Horses" = the things which are of the understanding. References.

@6125. "For horses" (Genesis 47:17) = scientifics from what is intellectual. "Horses" = intellectual things... and as they are predicated of Egypt... "horses" here = scientifics from what is intellectual. Explained, Illustrated.

@--[end]. That intelligence is to be acquired through the Word... and not through scientifics from man's Own Intellectual, is signified by, "The king shall not multiply horses, and shall not bring the people back into Egypt to multiply horses" (Deuteronomy 17:16).

@6212[2]. Afterwards I saw a horse, on which some one had been seated, who was thrown from the horse backwards, and there lay while the horse was kicking him: afterwards another was seen seated on a horse: the horses were noble ones. The Angels said... that the horse which threw its rider and kicked signified that the Jewish and Israelitish people, who had the prophecies, were merely in externals; and thus that the Intellectual rejected them, and as it were by kicking put them away: and that the other rider seated on a horses the Intellectual which those have who are in the internal sense of the prophetic Word.

@6400. "Biting the heels of the horse" = fallacies from lowest nature... "A horse" = what is intellectual; here, "the horse" = fallacies, because it is what is intellectual of the lowest Natural...

@6534[4]. That by "horses," and "riders," are signified intellectual things; and, in the opposite sense, reasonings and the derivative falsities. Illustrated.

@--. That here (Revelation 6) "the horses" and "those who sit on them" = such things as are of the understanding of truth; and, in the opposite sense, of falsity, is evident from the particulars. "The white horse and he who sat on him" = the understanding of truth from the Word... "the red horse and he who sat on him" = reasonings from the cupidities of evil, by which violence is inflicted on the truths from the Word; "the black horse and he who sat on him" = the understanding of truth extinguished; and "the pale horse and he who sat on him" = the consequent damnation.

@--[5]. "Horses" and "riders," in the opposite sense, = a perverted understanding and the derivative falsities. Illustrated.

@6952[3]. "The tails of the horses were like serpents"... (Revelation 9:19) = reasonings from falsities... for by "horses" is signified what is intellectual.

@7503. "Upon the horses, upon the donkeys, upon the camels" (Exodus 9:3) = the intellectual and scientific things of the truth which is of faith. "Horses" = intellectual things. References... These three animals = the things which are of the intellectual part. Explained.

@8029[end]. Bright horses as it were fiery = an enlightened understanding.

@8146[end]. "The horses of Pharaoh" (Exodus 14:23) = scientific falsities from a perverted Intellectual. @8156. @8210.

@8265. "The horse and his rider He hath cast into the sea" (Exodus 15:1) = that at His mere presence falsities from evil are condemned and cast into Hell. (8343.) "Horses" = falsities from a perverted Intellectual. That "a horse" = what is intellectual (References.); and, in the opposite sense, a perverted Intellectual; and as this is no Intellectual, in this sense "a horse" = falsity; and "the horse of Pharaoh," a scientific falsity.

@8313[3]. "They ride upon horses" (Jeremiah 6:23) = argumentation as from what is intellectual.

@8381. When the Spirits of Jupiter saw the horses of this Earth, the horses appeared to me smaller than usual... This was from the idea of the Spirits of that Earth concerning the horses there. They said that with them there were like ones, but much larger; and that they were wild or in the forests; and that when they are seen they terrify them, although they do them no harm... For, in the Spiritual World, a horse represents the Intellectual formed from scientifics; and as they fear to cultivate the Intellectual by means of knowledges, there is an influx of fear. @SE 560.

@8409[2]. "The horses of Egypt" (Isaiah 31:3) = scientifics from a perverted Intellectual.

@8906[3]. "The aspect of the horses" (Joel 2:4) = the Intellectual reasoning from falsity as if from truth.

@9391[17]. "The horse of the peoples" (Zechariah 12:4) = the intellectual things of truth with those who are of the Church.

@9396[11]. "Horse" = the understanding of the Word. References.

@9466[end]. "Horses and those who sit on them" (Revelation 9:17) = an inverted and perverted understanding of truth.

@9755[4]. To "tread the sea with horses," when said of Jehovah (Habakkuk 3:15) = to instruct the natural man, who has scientifics.

@9818[12]. "The horses of Egypt" (Isaiah 31:3) = scientifics from what is intellectual. References. ( = the Intellectual from the Scientific. @10283[10].)

@10033[2]. "Horse" (Ezekiel 39:20) = the internal sense of the Word.

